{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"I’ve settled on a fused layout-conversion kernel: one program handles all query heads for a token and another handles all key/value heads. That lets each launch compute RMS backward, RoPE backward, head reductions, and the transposed Q/K/V packing in one pass, while leaving the two large matrix multiplications to the tuned ROCm backend. I’ll validate this locally against `reference.py` before spending a verifier attempt."}}
