{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"The first permutation-based rewrite was correct but slower because cross-lane shuffles outweighed the saved loads. I’m replacing it with a paired-half formulation: each program carries the first and second 64-wide halves as separate tiles, so every RoPE partner is already in a register and no reload or lane shuffle is needed."}}
